{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789819874,"nonce":"N/Jih5z3kElT4nq1r9WIBcp7wjQ=","message":"Landed since the last note:\n\n- NativeLib sections (2ec1da1): the plugins in `plugins/` beside the program, for the building target, written to a temp dir and loaded from there by a bundle session. Hatch packages whole as `hatch` module sections (7786a5a), staged by wren_lift unchanged.\n- c569191bda33665317180f7b2a872b867f00d0c1: `SectionKind::Language` (kind 5) names a frontend the run brings up: `zsnap` with the snapshot bytes (a `.zyn` is compiled and wrapped in a snapshot of its grammar at build), `builtin` for a frontend in this build of caribou (Python; `project::builtin`). The driver reads these before building the world, since a language must be registered before `World::install` can hand it a module. Each language's modules ride as `source` module sections named by path under the root (`game/tally.py`); `caribou_zyntax::Runtime::install` stages them and the loader maps a module name through the language's `ModuleArchitecture` to the staged paths before the roots. `Language::parse` now takes a `Sources` handle so a frontend that resolves its own imports (Python's `import game.util`) reads staged sources too. `.zrtl` files in `plugins/` ride as NativeLib with lang `zyntax`; `bundle::native_libs` writes one directory per set of contents and both `caribou_plugin::load_dir` and the frontends read it. Test: crates/caribou-interop/tests/bundle_zyntax.rs (zynml.hl bundled with the ZynML snapshot and the Python module, opened from a temp dir; Haxe reaches Point, Wren reaches tally's score).\n\nStill here: resources a program can reach, Api sections, other targets' libs, docs, compression. Also Zyntax modules in compiled form: the snapshot already carries a module lowered to HIR with its declarations beside it (`SnapshotBuilder::module_lowered`, `CompiledImport`), which is the form to move to once the frontends settle; the loader would publish from the CompiledImport's declarations and compile its HIR. ZynML-to-ZynML imports inside a module are not resolved from roots or staged sources today (no import resolver is registered on the runtime for them); Python's are.","files":null}]}